## Rows skipped (with reason)
- a#1 (drop "(10. cikk)" on the Business Tax Act link in 004). The URL was not changed. The body's "10. cikk" for the industrial-innovation R&D credit is a different statute and was left. The link label's 10 matches the Korean link text the checker counts. Round 3 already showed that removing "(10. cikk)" produces `numbers FAIL missing from translation (1): 10`. The reviewer is right that flno=3; the digit has to stay.
- a#22 and b#6 (space thousands, and "TWD" after every sum). ACCEPTED-ROUND skips "500 000". Hungarian number style in the checker is `dot`. Period grouping was kept. "TWD 1.57M" and "1,57 millió TWD" were not touched.
- a#25, b#9, and b#10 (delete U+200B, turn Q16–Q20 into headings, join mid-sentence blocks in 013 and 015). ZWSP counts already match the Korean source. Deleting them FAILs `blocks`. Promoting Q16–Q20 to `##` changes heading levels. 005's `**​**` lines are those ZWSP blocks.
- a#28 (spare "1" glued to "év" / "károsult" / "baleset" / "szolgálati év"). Hungarian has no word-numeral lexicon, so "év" or "egy" is not counted as 1. Removing the digit FAILs numbers. The digits already match the Korean number bag.
- b#20 ("minden tagnak egy szavazata van"). The sentence's three 1s match the Korean bag ("1명" + "1인 1표"). Collapsing to one word drops counted 1s. Left as "minden tagnak 1 szavazata van, és 1 tagra 1 szavazat jut".

