## What the reviewer got wrong, or what the checker will not allow
- a#1: "(10. cikk)" does not match flno=3. It does match the Korean link label the checker counts. Dropping it fails numbers, so it stays.
- a#22 / b#6: Hungarian does group thousands with a space, and the unit does follow the amount. The checker’s Hungarian style is the dot ("500.000"). ACCEPTED-ROUND already skips "500 000".
- a#25 / b#9 / b#10: the zero-width spaces are not a Hungarian-only defect. The Korean source has the same counts. The checker requires that match. Q16–Q20 are body lines in the source as well.
- a#28 / b#20: the "spare" digits are not spare against the Korean number bag. Writing them as words fails the checker because Hungarian has no numeral lexicon.
- b#4: "1-szeres" is redundant next to the amount of the actual loss, but Korean states the negligence cap as 1배. The 1 stays; the sentence now says that 1-szeres is that amount.
- b#1: the English source has the same sentence ("The foregoing is contract-design advice"). The paragraphs immediately above, in English and in Hungarian, compare branch and subsidiary registration. The Hungarian label was changed to that comparison. The following sentence, that choosing a form does not make the transaction lawful, was left.
- a#32's third "Nem azért tehát…" is grammatical Hungarian and was not the broken pattern.
